    "result_text": "All imports are still used. The implementation is complete and the full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1/1 tests green).\n\n## Summary\n\nI released version 2 of the owner identity, keeping each concern in its own small unit:\n\n**Identity derivation (V2 tag mixed inside identifiers)**\n- New `util/IdentityVersion` \u2014 single home for the scheme: `CURRENT = 2`, the fixed `TAG = \"V2\"`, `regionCode(region)` (embeds the tag \u2192 e.g. `V2NSW`) and `plainRegion(code)` (strips it back \u2192 `NSW`).\n- `AssignMemberId` now embeds the V2 region code, so `memberId` becomes `V2NSW261A2B3C4D5\u2026` (disjoint from every V1 id).\n- `Households.householdId` and `IdentityKey.of` now salt their SHA-256 pre-image with the `V2` tag, so both digests change and no V1 value recurs.\n\n**Locality stays plain**\n- New `util/OwnerLocality.of(owner)` \u2014 the single derivation of the plain region: reads the REGION code off the member id and decodes the tag. Reused by both the mapper and the audit publisher, so `locality`, `timezone` and the owner segment's derived region never carry the tag.\n\n**Response shape**\n- `openapi.yml`: added top-level `apiVersion` (int 2) and an `identity` object (new `OwnerIdentity` schema holding `memberId`, `householdId`, `identityKey`); removed those three from the top level.\n- `OwnerMapper`: builds the nested `identity`, sets `apiVersion` from `IdentityVersion.CURRENT`, and `locality` now decodes via `OwnerLocality`.\n\n**Audit schema v2**\n- `OwnerCreatedEvent` gained `schemaVersion` (2) and `ownerSegment`; `OwnerEventPublisher` recomputes the segment from the V2 identity (`OwnerSegment.of(level, OwnerLocality.of(owner))`), computing the membership level once.\n\nRequest fields are unchanged. Verified live: `memberId=V2NSW2616E6609E9`, audit `{\"\u2026\",\"ownerSegment\":\"STANDARD_METRO\",\"schemaVersion\":2,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}`, and the segment `STANDARD_METRO` confirms locality decodes back to the plain `NSW`.",
