    "probe_text": "I've read the endpoint YAML and every function class in the pipeline. Here is the complete ordered sequence for `POST /api/owners`, exactly as the code executes it. I've marked each step as a **validation** (can reject the request) or a **side-effect** (mutates state / emits output).\n\n## Gate (before the pipeline)\n0. **[validation] Authorization** \u2014 `composition.authorize: hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`. Without that role the request is rejected before any step runs.\n\n## Idempotency branch\n1. **CheckIdempotencyKey** \u2014 reads the `Idempotency-Key` header. If the key was seen by a prior create, it takes the `replay` branch \u2192 **LoadReplayedOwner** loads the originally created owner and **RespondWithOwner** returns it with **200**, bypassing the entire create pipeline. No key, or an unseen key, falls through to create.\n\n## Validations (in order, each a 4xx before anything is built or saved)\n2. **[side-effect + validation] ValidateOwnerFields** \u2014 first canonicalizes the address in place (prefers `addressLine1/2`, else flat `address`, writing the composed value back to `address`), then requires `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` to be non-blank \u2192 **400** (`MissingOwnerFieldsException`). Republishes the body for later steps.\n3. **[validation + normalization] NormalizeOwnerTelephone** \u2014 converts `telephone` to E.164 and mutates the DTO; unconvertible \u2192 **400** (`InvalidTelephoneException`).\n4. **[validation + normalization] NormalizeOwnerEmail** \u2014 email optional; when present must be syntactically valid (\u2192 **400** `InvalidEmailException`) and is stored lower-cased.\n5. **[validation] RejectDisposableEmail** \u2014 email optional; when present, a domain on the disposable blocklist \u2192 **400** (`DisposableEmailException`).\n6. **[validation] ValidateOwnerPostcode** \u2014 postcode optional; when present must be exactly 4 digits and (for a city with a known region) within that region's range \u2192 **400** (`InvalidPostcodeException`). Value left unchanged.\n7. **[validation] ValidateRegistrationDate** \u2014 date optional; when supplied must not be after the server's current date \u2192 **400** (`FutureRegistrationDateException`).\n8. **[validation] EnsureUniqueIdentity** *(transaction)* \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold=true`, rejects if the identity key (SHA-256 over normalized telephone + lower-cased email + last-name Soundex) matches any non-deleted existing owner \u2192 **409** (`DuplicateIdentityException`).\n9. **[validation] EnsureCityCapacity** *(transaction)* \u2014 rejects if the city already holds the max owners \u2192 **409** (`CityCapacityExceededException`).\n10. **[side-effect] ResolveRegistrationDate** \u2014 computes the effective date (supplied, else today), rolls a weekend forward to the next business day, and publishes it as a variable.\n11. **[validation] EnsureDailyLimit** *(transaction)* \u2014 rejects if \u2265 100 owners are already registered on the *resolved* business day \u2192 **429** (`DailyLimitExceededException`).\n\n## Build & stamp the entity (side-effects, all under `transaction`)\n12. **BuildOwner** \u2014 maps the validated DTO to an `Owner` entity.\n13. **ApplyRegistrationDate** \u2014 stamps the owner with the resolved business-day date, overwriting any date mapped from the body.\n14. **AssignMemberId** \u2014 computes and sets `memberId` = `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` (region code via `IdentityVersion`/`OwnerRegion`, 2-digit fiscal year of the registration date, first 8 hex of SHA-256(telephone+lastName), Luhn check digit); collisions with existing member ids are de-duplicated by appending `-<n>`.\n15. **AssignHousehold** \u2014 sets `householdId` = first 12 hex of SHA-256(lastName, postcode); left unset when there's no postcode.\n16. **AssignMembershipLevelCap** \u2014 if the household already has members, sets `membershipLevelCap` = (max existing member level) + 1; otherwise unset.\n17. **AssignHouseholdSize** \u2014 sets `householdSize` = existing members sharing the `householdId` + 1.\n18. **AssignNamesakeCount** \u2014 sets `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners sharing the same first+last name (case-insensitive), excluding the new owner.\n19. **AssignPossibleDuplicate** \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold=true` (then flag forced false/null), sets `possibleDuplicate=true` and `possibleDuplicateOf=<id>` for the first non-deleted existing owner with the same non-blank postcode and last-name Soundex but a *different* identity key; else false/null.\n\n## Persist & emit (side-effects, all under `transaction`)\n20. **SaveOwner** \u2014 persists the owner (assigns its generated id).\n21. **RecordIdempotencyKey** \u2014 if the request carried an `Idempotency-Key`, stores `key \u2192 owner id` for future replays.\n22. **AuditOwnerCreated** \u2014 logs `id, memberId, registrationDate, membershipLevel` to the `AUDIT` logger.\n23. **EmitOwnerCreatedEvent** \u2014 publishes the structured `OWNER_CREATED` event (with monotonic sequence) via `OwnerEventPublisher` to the `AUDIT` logger.\n24. **EnqueueWelcomeNotification** \u2014 logs a welcome line (`owner id`, `memberId`) to the `NOTIFY` logger.\n\n## Response\n25. **RespondWithOwnerCreated** \u2014 builds the `OwnerDto` (via `OwnerResponses.toDto`, which computes the response's membership level, etc.) and sends **201 Created** with a `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header.\n\n---\n\nTwo notes from reading the actual code (vs. the YAML comments):\n- The transaction governance spans steps 8\u201325 (every step from `EnsureUniqueIdentity` onward carries `govern: [ transaction ]`), so all the DB reads used for uniqueness/capacity/limit checks and the final save commit as one unit at the end.\n- The code matches the described behavior; the only cosmetic drift is the `memberId` region format \u2014 the YAML comment describes a plain `<REGION>` prefix, while `AssignMemberId`/`IdentityVersion` actually emit a version-tagged `V2<region>` code (e.g. `V2NSW\u2026`)."
